"Claude Platform release notes - Claude Platform Docs (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/overview)\nciteturn31565view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/overview\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 901\nL0: cite0†Claude Platform Docs L1: \nL2:   * cite1†Messages L3:   * cite2†Managed Agents L4:   * cite3†Admin L5:   * Resources\nL6:     * cite4†Best practices L7:     * cite5†Models & pricing L8:     * cite6†SDKs, CLI, and libraries L9:     * cite7†Claude API skill L10:     * cite8†Release notes L11: \nL12: \nL13: \nL14: Search`Ctrl``K`\nL15: \nL16: Release notes\nL17: \nL18: cite8†Overview L19: \nL20: Migration guides\nL21: \nL22: cite9†Migrating to Managed Agents L23: \nL24: cite10†Console L25: \nL26: Release notes\nL27: # Claude Platform release notes\nL28: \nL29: Updates to the Claude Platform, including the Claude API, client SDKs, and the Claude Console.\nL30: \nL31: cite11†Subscribe L32: \nL33: Copy page\nL34: \nL35: \nL36: \nL37: The Claude Platform release notes list changes to the Claude API, the client SDKs, and the Claude Console, newest first.\nL38: \nL39: \nL40: \nL41: For release notes on Claude Apps, see the cite12†Release notes for Claude Apps in the Claude Help Center†support.claude.com .\nL42: For updates to Claude Code, see the cite13†complete CHANGELOG.md†github.com in the `claude-code` repository.\nL43: ### October 8, 2026\nL44: \nL45:   * The cite14†Compliance API chat endpoints now also return chats from the unified Claude experience, in beta for Claude Enterprise organizations, with your existing Compliance Access Key. See cite15†Retrieve and delete chats, files, and projects .\nL46: ### October 7, 2026\nL47:   * We've lowered the price of prompt cache reads on Claude Sonnet 5.5 from $0.20 USD to $0.10 USD per million tokens: 0.05x the base input price instead of 0.1x. Cache writes and all other prices are unchanged. See cite16†Prompt caching pricing .\nL48:   * We've launched Claude Haiku 5.5 (`claude-haiku-5-5`), our most capable model tuned for high-volume and latency-sensitive work. It has a cite17†1M token context window , 128k max output tokens, and cite18†adaptive thinking with the cite19†effort parameter . It's available on the Claude API, cite20†Claude in Amazon Bedrock , cite21†Claude Platform on AWS , cite22†Claude on Google Cloud , and cite23†Claude in Microsoft Foundry . See cite24†What's new in Claude Haiku 5.5 .\nL49:   * Code written for Claude Haiku 4.5 can break on Claude Haiku 5.5. Manual extended thinking (`budget_tokens`) returns a 400 error, and adaptive thinking is on by default, so a response can begin with `thinking` blocks. The same text also counts as more tokens. See the cite25†migration guide . For model-specific prompting patterns, see cite26†Prompting Claude Haiku 5.5 .\nL50:   * The Python and TypeScript SDKs now include classes, in beta, for the cite27†browser use tool and the cite28†computer use tool . You subclass one and write one method per tool against your own browser or desktop automation. The SDK runs the tool loop, the URL and file policies you set for the browser, and your approval callback. See cite29†Browser and computer use with the SDK toolsets .\nL51:   * Claude Max and Team plans now include monthly API credits. To learn how to claim them, see cite30†API credits for Max and Team plans .\nL52:   * In Claude Managed Agents, a cloud environment with `limited` networking now also applies its `allowed_hosts` to the `web_search` and `web_fetch` tools. A `web_fetch` call for a URL on a host that `allowed_hosts` does not match returns a `url_not_allowed` error result to the agent. `web_search` omits results from such hosts. When `allowed_hosts` lists no hosts, neither tool returns a page or a search result. `allow_package_managers` and `allow_mcp_servers` add no hosts for these tools.\nL53: To let the tools reach a host, add it to `allowed_hosts`, which also opens it to the sandbox. `unrestricted` networking and self-hosted environments do not limit these tools. See cite31†Environment networking .\nL54:   * With `limited` networking, creating a session fails with a 400 error when an enabled web tool's `allowed_domains` has an entry not within `allowed_hosts`. So does a session update that adds such an entry. An `allowed_hosts` entry matches one exact host unless it starts with `*.`, so `docs.example.com` is not within `[\"example.com\"]`. To fix the error, add the host to `allowed_hosts` or remove the entry from `allowed_domains`. See cite32†Restrict web search and web fetch domains .\nL55:   * In Claude Managed Agents, the cite33†`web_fetch` tool now fetches only URLs that have already appeared in the session, for example in the text of a user message, in a `web_search` result, or in a page that `web_fetch` returned earlier. This reduces the risk of data exfiltration.\nL56: A URL that appears only in Claude's own output, the agent's system prompt, an attached document, or the output of a tool such as `bash`, `read`, or an MCP tool does not count: a `web_fetch` call for it returns a `url_not_in_prior_context` error result to the agent. To let the agent fetch a URL, send it in the text of a `user.message` event.\nL57: ### October 6, 2026\nL58: \nL59:   * We've added `capabilities.server_tools` to the cite34†Models API . `GET /v1/models` and `GET /v1/models/{model_id}` now report whether each model accepts the web search and code execution tools. To check whether a model accepts the code execution tool, read `capabilities.server_tools.code_execution`. The top-level `capabilities.code_execution` reports whether code can call your request's other tools. See cite35†Using the Models API .\nL60: ### October 5, 2026\nL61: \nL62:   * We've added `capabilities.thinking.types.disabled` to the cite34†Models API . `GET /v1/models` and `GET /v1/models/{model_id}` now report whether each model accepts `thinking: {type: \"disabled\"}`, which turns thinking off. See cite35†Using the Models API .\nL63: ### October 1, 2026\nL64:   * We've added a `line` field to the cite34†Models API . `GET /v1/models` and `GET /v1/models/{model_id}` now return the model line each model belongs to. Claude Opus 4.5 and Claude Opus 4.6 both report `opus`, for example. Use `line` to group models without parsing their IDs. `line` is `null` for a model that belongs to no line. See cite35†Using the Models API .\nL65:   * cite36†Dreams (research preview) now supports Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Fable 5.1, and Claude Sonnet 5.5. See cite37†Supported models .\nL66: ### September 30, 2026\nL67:   * In Python SDK 1.10.0, TypeScript SDK 0.130.0, C# SDK 12.52.0, Go SDK 1.77.0, Java SDK 2.67.0, PHP SDK 0.53.0, Ruby SDK 1.75.0, and version 1.37.0 of the `ant` CLI, the cite3†Admin API methods for organization info, members, invites, workspaces, API keys, rate limits, service accounts, workload identity federation, customer-managed encryption keys, and compliance settings are out of beta: call them under `client.organization` and `ant organization`.\nL68: These releases also keep `client.beta.organization` and `ant beta:organization`.\nL69:   * We announced the deprecation of the Claude Sonnet 4.5 model (`claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929`), with retirement on the Claude API scheduled for November 30, 2026. We recommend migrating to cite38†Claude Sonnet 5.5 . Read more in cite39†Model deprecations .\nL70: ### September 28, 2026\nL71:   * We've launched Claude Sonnet 5.5 (`claude-sonnet-5-5`). It's available on the Claude API, cite20†Claude in Amazon Bedrock , cite21†Claude Platform on AWS , cite22†Claude on Google Cloud , and cite23†Claude in Microsoft Foundry . For its context window, output limits, and prices, see the cite40†Claude Sonnet 5.5 model page .\nL72:   * Code written for Claude Sonnet 5 can break on Claude Sonnet 5.5 in five ways. To turn off up-front thinking, send `thinking: {\"type\": \"between_tools\"}` instead of `\"disabled\"`, at `high` effort or below. Forced tool use (`tool_choice` types `any` and `tool`) returns a 400 error. Thinking blocks are tied to the model and the conversation. On the Claude API and Google Cloud, the earlier `computer_20251124` computer use tool isn't accepted.\nL73: The advisor tool rejects Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, and Claude Sonnet 5 as advisors. See cite41†What's new in Claude Sonnet 5.5 for each change and the cite42†migration guide for before-and-after requests. For model-specific prompting patterns, see cite43†Prompting Claude Sonnet 5.5 .\nL74:   * Thinking blocks that Claude Sonnet 5.5 produces work only in the account that produced them, or in an account linked to it. When another account sends one of these blocks, the API drops the block before the model sees it, and the request succeeds. Blocks from earlier models aren't affected. See cite44†Preserved thinking .\nL75: ### September 24, 2026\nL76:   * We're resuming billing for refusals that arrive before any output when `stop_details.category` is `\"bio\"`, `\"frontier_llm\"`, or `\"reasoning_extraction\"`, the categories where we measure low volumes of false positives. Mid-stream refusals were already billed. Refusals billed under this change are charged like any other request, at the rates of the model that ran it. Refusals before any output in other categories are still not billed, and fallback credit is unchanged.\nL77: This change applies on all platforms. See cite45†How refusals are billed .\nL78:   * The cite14†Compliance API local session endpoints are out of beta for Claude for Microsoft 365 sessions in Excel, PowerPoint, Word, and Outlook (`product_surface` values beginning with `office_agents`). See cite46†Sessions on users' machines .\nL79:   * The cite14†Compliance API cite47†Activity Feed no longer returns file names, project document names, or artifact titles. The `filename` and `title` fields on file, project document, and artifact activities are now always empty or omitted, including on activities recorded before this change. To look up a name or title by the ID on the activity, use a Compliance Access Key with the `read:compliance_user_data` scope. See cite48†Understand the Activity object .\nL80: ### September 23, 2026\nL81: \nL82:   * cite49†Cache diagnostics is out of beta on the Claude API and no longer requires the `cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07` beta header. Include the `diagnostics` object on a Messages request to opt in; requests that still send the header work as before. Responses from `POST /v1/messages` now always include the `diagnostics` field, which is `null` when the request did not include the `diagnostics` object.\nL83: ### September 22, 2026\nL84:   * We've launched Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`), a model for long-running agentic coding and knowledge work. It has a cite17†1M token context window by default, 128k max output tokens, and always-on cite18†adaptive thinking , at $4 / $20 USD per MTok (Claude Opus 5 is $5 / $25). Claude Opus 5.5 is available on the Claude API, cite20†Claude in Amazon Bedrock , cite21†Claude Platform on AWS , cite22†Claude on Google Cloud , and cite23†Claude in Microsoft Foundry .\nL85: See cite50†What's new in Claude Opus 5.5 for capabilities, API changes, and migration guidance.\nL86:   * On Claude Opus 5.5, thinking can't be disabled: `thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"}` and `thinking: {\"type\": \"enabled\", ...}` return a 400 error. Omit the `thinking` field and control thinking depth with the cite19†effort parameter . `tool_choice` types `any` and `tool` also return a 400 error, as on Claude Fable 5.1; use `auto` with cite51†strict tool use .\nL87: On the Claude API and Google Cloud, cite28†computer use on this model requires the `computer_toolset_20260801` toolset and the earlier `computer_20251124` tool returns a 400 error; on Amazon Bedrock, `computer_20251124` keeps working. See the cite52†migration guide .\nL88:   * cite53†Fast mode (research preview) is available for Claude Opus 5.5 on the Claude API.\nL89:   * Tools can now be defined inside a cite54†mid-conversation system message , in beta on the Claude API with the `inline-tools-2026-09-15` beta header. A `tool_addition` block can carry the tool's full definition (`tool: {\"type\": \"tool_definition\", \"definition\": {...}}`), so you can add a tool, change its schema, or move a server tool to a newer version without editing `tools` or invalidating the prompt cache. The same header covers adding and removing tools by reference.\nL90: With the MCP connector's `mcp-client-2026-09-15` beta header as well, the definition can be an MCP toolset, and a response records each server's fetched tool list in an `mcp_tool_listing` block, which pins that list when you send it back.\nL91: ### September 18, 2026\nL92:   * For cite49†cache diagnostics , a response to a request that sends the `cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07` beta header now always includes the `diagnostics` field. The field is `null` when the request did not include the `diagnostics` object. Previously the field was omitted in that case.\nL93:   * The cite14†Compliance API local session endpoints now also return transcripts of Claude in Chrome sessions (`product_surface` value `claude_in_chrome`), in beta for Claude Enterprise organizations, with your existing Compliance Access Key and the `read:compliance_user_data` scope. See cite46†Sessions on users' machines .\nL94: ### September 14, 2026\nL95:   * The Messages API can now cite55†compact a conversation on demand on the Claude API, in beta with the `compact-2026-09-04` beta header. Send the top-level `compaction` parameter, and the API returns a signed `compaction` block that summarizes the messages you sent. On later requests, send that block first, in place of those messages. You choose when to compact, the request can run in the background, and you can keep recent turns word for word after the summary.\nL96: On models with preserved thinking, the thinking in those kept turns can stay valid.\nL97:   * With the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header, the `input_transformations` response field gains a second entry type, `thinking_mismatch_allowed`. It names a thinking block that failed the prefix check on a request where the API doesn't enforce that check: on Claude Fable 5.1, for example, a request from an account created before August 31, 2026, with `prefix_mismatch_behavior` unset. The block still reaches the model unchanged.\nL98: Log these entries to find history edits in production traffic before you opt into enforcement. See cite56†Set the mismatch behavior and read `input_transformations` .\nL99: ### September 10, 2026\nL100:   * Claude Managed Agents permission policies now include `auto`: the server evaluates each agent or MCP tool call and runs it, denies it, or pauses for your approval. `agent.tool_use` and `agent.mcp_tool_use` events report how each call was evaluated in an `evaluation` field alongside `evaluated_permission`. See cite57†Let the server evaluate each call with `auto` .\nL101:   * Version 1.32.0 of the `ant` CLI adds `ant beta:sessions connect`, which attaches your terminal to a Claude Managed Agents session. You can follow the session live, send messages, and allow or deny tool calls that are waiting for approval. Pass `--web` to serve the Claude Console's session viewer locally and open the session there instead. See cite58†Connect to a Managed Agents session from your terminal .\nL102: ### September 9, 2026\nL103: \nL104:   * For cite49†cache diagnostics , the API now stores a request's fingerprint only when the request includes the `diagnostics` object. A request that sends only the `cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07` beta header is still accepted, but no fingerprint is stored. A later turn that points `previous_message_id` at it reports `previous_message_not_found`. Include `diagnostics` on every turn, with `\"previous_message_id\": null` on the first.\nL105: ### September 3, 2026\nL106:   * Version 1.30.0 of the `ant` CLI adds `ant apply`, which creates and updates agents, environments, skills, memory stores, and deployments from files in your repository. Describe each resource in a file, run `ant apply`, and approve the plan it prints. Commit the `claude-lock.json` lockfile it writes so that later runs, on your machine or in CI, update the same resources instead of creating new ones. See cite59†Manage resources as code with ant apply .\nL107:   * cite60†Per-message effort changes, in beta, are also available on cite22†Google Cloud for Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, and Claude Opus 5, with the same `mid-conversation-output-config-2026-07-01` beta header.\nL108: ### September 1, 2026\nL109:   * We've launched Claude Fable 5.1 (`claude-fable-5-1`), the successor to Claude Fable 5 for long-running agentic coding, knowledge work, and research, alongside Claude Mythos 5.1 (`claude-mythos-5-1`) for Project Glasswing participants. Both models support a cite17†1M token context window by default, 128k max output tokens, and always-on cite18†adaptive thinking , at $10 / $50 USD per MTok, the same as Claude Fable 5, with cache reads cut to $0.25 per MTok.\nL110: Claude Fable 5.1 is available on the Claude API, cite20†Claude in Amazon Bedrock , cite21†Claude Platform on AWS , cite22†Claude on Google Cloud , and cite23†Claude in Microsoft Foundry . See cite61†What's new in Claude Fable 5.1 for capabilities, API changes, and migration guidance.\nL111:   * Prompt cache reads on Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 cost $0.25 USD per million tokens: 0.025x the base input price, compared with 0.1x on other models. Cache writes are unchanged. See cite16†Prompt caching pricing .\nL112:   * On Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1, `tool_choice` types `any` and `tool` aren't supported and return a 400 error. `auto` and `none` are unchanged. To guarantee schema-conformant tool inputs, use cite51†strict tool use or cite62†structured outputs .\nL113:   * Thinking blocks produced by Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 are preserved only for the model that produced them or a newer one: earlier models can't read them, and the API drops one replayed to an earlier model. Claude Fable 5.1 accepts thinking blocks from Claude Opus 5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Mythos 5, and earlier Claude models.\nL114: On Claude Fable 5.1, the API also cite63†checks that nothing before a block has changed : for new accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, replaying one after the `system` prompt, `tools`, or an earlier message changed returns a 400 error. With the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header, dropped blocks are reported in an `input_transformations` response field, and `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior` chooses between rejecting and dropping blocks whose history changed.\nL115: See cite64†Preserved thinking .\nL116:   * Per-message effort changes are in beta on Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, and Claude Opus 5 on the Claude API. Add a `role: \"system\"` message with `output_config.effort` inside `messages` to change effort for later turns while preserving the prompt cache. Include the `mid-conversation-output-config-2026-07-01` beta header in your requests. See cite60†Per-message effort .\nL117:   * cite65†Turn-scoped system messages are in beta (`mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21` header). Set `clear_at: \"next_user_message\"` on a mid-conversation `role: \"system\"` message and it renders for the current turn only, then stays in the history at no token cost. Per-turn reminders don't accumulate and don't invalidate the prompt cache or later thinking blocks.\nL118:   * `thinking.display` accepts a third value, `\"updates\"`, in beta (`thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18` header). Reasoning comes back with an empty `thinking` field, as under `\"omitted\"`, and the short progress updates that Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, and Claude Fable 5 write between tool calls come back as text, at most one `thinking` block before a tool call. See cite66†Progress updates between tool calls .\nL119:   * Text generated by Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 carries Anthropic's text watermark, and supported image, video, and audio files that Claude produces through the cite67†code execution tool carry C2PA Content Credentials when you retrieve them through the cite68†Files API on the Claude API. Marking requires no changes to your requests or response handling.\nL120:   * Like Claude Fable 5, both models require 30-day data retention and aren't available under zero data retention unless expressly authorized by Anthropic. See cite69†Model-specific data retention requirements .\nL121:   * The guides for the Claude Enterprise endpoints of the cite70†Admin API (cite71†user management and cite72†spend limits ), the cite73†Claude Enterprise Analytics API , and the cite14†Compliance API now show the `anthropic-version` header; send it on every request to these endpoints, as in the rest of the Claude API. See cite74†API versions .\nL122: ### August 27, 2026\nL123:   * In Python SDK 1.2.0, TypeScript SDK 0.122.0, Go SDK 1.68.0, Java SDK 2.59.0, Ruby SDK 1.67.0, and C# SDK 12.44.0, `client.beta.files` and `client.beta.skills` no longer send the `files-api-2025-04-14` and `skills-2025-10-02` beta headers and return the same shapes as `client.files` and `client.skills`. With this change, `client.beta.skills.delete()` deletes a Skill together with all of its versions, and the beta Messages type `BetaSkill` (the container Skill reference) is renamed `BetaContainerSkill`.\nL124: Requests that still send the beta headers keep receiving the beta shapes. See cite75†Migrate from `files-api-2025-04-14` and cite76†Migrate from `skills-2025-10-02` .\nL125:   * You can now create personal keys and service account keys in the Claude Console. They act as you or as a cite77†service account , with the same permissions, and stop working when the linked account is removed from an organization. This lets organization admins more easily track usage for each account, and ensure key usage is legitimate. These API keys can be scoped to a specific workspace or cite78†work on admin endpoints and across any workspace the account has access to.\nL126: Workspace API keys remain supported as a legacy option. See cite79†API keys for more information.\nL127: ### August 26, 2026\nL128:   * The cite14†Compliance API session endpoints are out of beta for Cowork and Claude Code sessions. See cite80†Retrieve session transcripts .\nL129:   * The cite14†Compliance API local session endpoints now also return transcripts of Claude Science sessions (`product_surface` value `claude_science`) and Claude for Microsoft 365 sessions in Excel, PowerPoint, Word, and Outlook (`product_surface` values beginning with `office_agents`), in beta for Claude Enterprise organizations, with your existing Compliance Access Key and the `read:compliance_user_data` scope. See cite46†Sessions on users' machines .\nL130:   * The cite3†Admin API is now available in the `ant` CLI and the Python, TypeScript, C#, Go, Java, PHP, and Ruby SDKs under `client.beta.organization`. They cover organization info, members, invites, workspaces and workspace members, API keys, rate limits, service accounts, workload identity federation issuers and rules, and customer-managed encryption keys. Usage and cost reports and the Claude Enterprise user-management and analytics endpoints remain curl-only.\nL131: The CLI and SDKs read an Admin API key from `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or an `org:admin` OAuth token from `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`.\nL132: ### August 20, 2026\nL133:   * We've released v1.0 of the cite81†Python SDK . The SDK's HTTP layer moves from `httpx` to cite82†httpx2†httpx2.pydantic.dev , a maintained, API-compatible fork: build custom `http_client`, `Timeout`, and transport objects from `httpx2` (the `DefaultHttpxClient` helpers are unchanged), and call `httpx2.alias_httpx()` at startup if you rely on tracing or mocking libraries that patch `httpx`.\nL134: v1.0 requires Python 3.10 or later and removes long-deprecated surface, including the legacy Text Completions API, the `temperature`, `top_p`, and `top_k` parameters on Messages methods, and the tool runner's client-side `compaction_control`. On the async client, `.with_raw_response` results now need `await response.parse()`, and `AnthropicBedrock` now raises an error when no AWS region is configured instead of defaulting to `us-east-1`.\nL135: See the cite83†v1 migration guide†github.com for every change with before-and-after snippets.\nL136:   * The cite28†computer use and cite27†browser use toolsets (`computer_toolset_20260801` and `browser_toolset_20260801`) are now available on cite22†Google Cloud for Claude Fable 5, Claude Mythos 5, Claude Opus 5, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Opus 4.8. Requests use the same `tools` entries as on the Claude API.\nL137: ### August 19, 2026\nL138:   * The cite28†computer use tool is out of beta on the Claude API as the `computer_toolset_20260801` toolset: no beta header, batch actions (several actions in one turn), `zoom` enabled by default, and per-member configuration through `configs`. Earlier beta versions remain available. Upgrading an existing integration changes the request shape and tool handling; see cite84†Migrate from `computer_20251124` .\nL139:   * We've launched the cite27†browser use tool (`browser_toolset_20260801`), a client toolset for driving a browser that your application hosts. It works inside a browser viewport rather than a whole desktop, reading the page itself (its accessibility tree, elements, forms, and tabs) and adding element references, form input, tab management, download reporting, and opt-in file upload on top of screenshot-and-click control.\nL140:   * Both toolsets are available for Claude Fable 5, Claude Mythos 5, Claude Opus 5, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Opus 4.8 on the Claude API.\nL141:   * The cite68†Files API is out of beta on the Claude API. Requests to the `/v1/files` endpoints, and Messages API requests that reference an uploaded file, no longer require the `files-api-2025-04-14` beta header. Requests sent without the header use the current response format: cite85†file expiration (set `expires_in_seconds` when you upload a file; file objects report `expires_at`), and `page` and `next_page` cite86†pagination plus an `ids[]` filter when you cite87†list files .\nL142: `/v1/files` requests that still send the beta header keep working and return the previous response format. To move an existing integration off the header, see cite75†Migrate from `files-api-2025-04-14` .\nL143:   * cite88†Agent Skills and the Skills API (`/v1/skills`) are out of beta on the Claude API. Requests no longer require the `skills-2025-10-02` beta header, including Messages API requests that load Skills through the `container` parameter. Requests that still send the header continue to work unchanged. See cite89†Using Agent Skills with the API . To move an existing integration off the header, see cite76†Migrate from `skills-2025-10-02` .\nL144:   * The cite70†Admin API user-management endpoints for Claude Enterprise (claude.ai) organizations (members, invites, groups, and custom roles) are out of beta. The `anthropic-beta: ce-user-management-2026-07-13` header is no longer required on group and custom-role requests; requests that still send it are accepted unchanged. See cite71†User management .\nL145:   * You can now restrict which sites a Claude Managed Agents agent's `web_search` and `web_fetch` tools can reach. Set `allowed_domains` or `blocked_domains` on the tool's entry in the `agent_toolset_20260401` `configs` array; `web_fetch` also accepts `max_content_tokens` and `web_search` accepts `user_location`.\nL146: Each `configs` entry is identified by its `name` and typed by an optional `type`, and requests that pass only `name`, `enabled`, and `permission_policy` continue to work; in the typed SDKs, `configs` entries become cite90†per-tool types . See cite32†Restrict web search and web fetch domains .\nL147:   * Claude Managed Agents sessions that run in a cite91†self-hosted sandbox can now attach cite92†memory stores . The Python, TypeScript, and Go SDK workers download each attached store into the sandbox at its `mount_path` and sync the agent's changes back to the store. See cite93†Memory stores in self-hosted sandboxes .\nL148:   * The session viewer in the Claude Console has been redesigned with a timeline minimap, a transcript grouped by model request, and an Inspector panel for session details and cost, raw events, per-tool statistics, mounted resources, and per-thread activity. See cite94†Inspect a session in the Console .\nL149: ### August 18, 2026\nL150: \nL151:   * Workbench is now cite95†playground in the Claude Console. Playground supports every Messages API parameter and includes templates that demonstrate API features such as code execution and web search. It shows the full SDK request and the API response for each run, to help you understand the API and build with it. For more, see the cite96†Claude Help Center†support.claude.com or try it at cite95†platform.claude.com/playground .\nL152: ### August 11, 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFast mode (research preview) - Claude Platform Docs (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/fast-mode)\nciteturn31565view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/fast-mode\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 355\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpeed up responses with fast mode - Claude Code Docs (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/fast-mode)\nciteturn31565view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/fast-mode\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 240\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn31565view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/2026-02?skip=450&show=100\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nComputation and Language Feb 2026 (https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CL/2026-02?show=100&skip=400)\nciteturn31565view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CL/2026-02?skip=400&show=100\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 933\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn31565view5 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.DC/2026-02?skip=50&show=50\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn31565view6 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CV/2026-02?skip=450&show=100\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n"
